course: dictionary
lesson: 881
title: Naming animals from context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some animals have names that sound like other animals. The binturong is also called a bearcat, but it is neither a bear nor a cat. A name can be a clue, but it can also mislead you, so read on and check the words around it.
explain: Look at this sentence: «The binturong, or bearcat, is an Asian tree animal whose urine smells like buttered popcorn because it holds the same chemical.» The word «or» tells you that bearcat is another name for the same animal. «Asian» and «tree animal» are clues about where it lives and where it spends its time.
explain: Clues can also tell you what an animal does. «It has a gripping tail» and «a binturong leaves a smell of buttered popcorn along its branch» show that it moves through trees. To test your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you are probably right.
fact: A binturong is a furry, dark animal from the rainforests of South-East Asia.
fact: The binturong is also called a bearcat, but it is neither a bear nor a cat.
fact: A binturong lives mostly in trees and can hold on with its long tail, which is called a prehensile (gripping) tail.
fact: It eats fruit and small animals.
fact: It is famous for smelling like buttered popcorn, and this smell comes from a chemical in its scent.
exercise: In «The binturong, or bearcat, is an Asian tree animal», what does «or bearcat» tell you? | *It is another name for the binturong | It is a cat that eats popcorn | It is a kind of tree | It is a bear from Asia
exercise: Why might the name bearcat mislead you? | It is a real bear that smells of popcorn | It is a big cat that lives in the desert | *It sounds like a bear or a cat, but the binturong is neither | It is a fish with a long tail
exercise: What does the binturong's gripping tail help it do? | Fly between the trees | *Hold on to branches while it moves in trees | Swim across rivers | Dig deep holes in the ground
test: Which word in «The binturong, or bearcat, is an Asian tree animal» tells you where it lives? | bearcat | animal | popcorn | *Asian
test: Read «a binturong leaves a smell of buttered popcorn along its branch.» What does this tell you about the binturong? | It is shy and rarely moves | *It spends time in trees, moving along branches | It is a fish that swims in ponds | It cannot climb at all
exam: Using the clues that it lives mostly in trees, eats fruit and small animals, and is called a bearcat, what is a binturong? | A bear that lives in the snow | *A furry, dark animal from the rainforests of South-East Asia that lives mostly in trees | A cat that lives in cities | A kind of popcorn sold in shops
